class_name WikiChapel
extends RefCounted
## Wiki page for the chapel (DVW-B3-CHAPEL): the clergy, offerings, asking for help and the church's plot. Every statement is
## taken from the code named beside it (Chapel, FarmPlots.plan_church, NPCBrain._plan_evening); numbers come from balance.json
## "chapel" (GameData.b). Registered by one line in Wiki.build.


static func add_pages(w: Wiki) -> void:
	var c: Dictionary = GameData.b("chapel")
	w.add_page("sys:chapel", "The chapel", "systems", [
		Wiki.p("The village has a small chapel east of Mill Road, between the sawmill's yard and the smithy, with a small fenced farm plot of its own next to it. Two villagers keep it: a preacher and a church assistant. Both are paid, but little: %d and %d coins a day, against %d for a manor hand. Their wage comes only from what the village gives the chapel. On a day the chapel's fund cannot pay, the wage is owed and paid when there is money again, for up to %d days, and nothing is made to pay it." % [int(c.wage.preacher), int(c.wage.church_assistant), int(GameData.b("manor_wage_per_day")), int(c.owed_days)]),
		Wiki.h("Offerings"),
		Wiki.p("Once a week, at the chapel's service, villagers may give. Giving is each person's own choice, made afresh every week: nothing is ever taken from anyone, and nobody thinks the worse of someone who gives nothing. Each villager is more or less devout, a fixed trait, and the devout give more often, but a devout villager may keep their coins in a hard week and one of little faith may give in a good one. How much they can spare, how many children or old folk their household feeds, and what they think of the preacher all weigh too. Only coins above what their household will need for the next few days, and a little savings, are ever given, and the amount varies; someone with nothing to spare is not asked. Households decide the same way whether to give some of the wheat they hold beyond what they need to eat. The coins go into the chapel's fund and the food into its store."),
		Wiki.p("You can give too. Talk to the preacher or the church assistant and choose to give coins or a piece of food. The chapel takes only food and seed corn, not goods."),
		Wiki.h("Asking for help"),
		Wiki.p("Everything given to the chapel is the first money and food used against hunger. When a household is running short of food, one of its members goes to the chapel and asks. The church fills the household's pantry from its store first, grain first; if its store runs short, it buys food from the villagers who have some to sell, with its own fund. Only then, if the household is still short, does the manor's relief step in, and it gives only what the church did not (see the manor's treasury and relief). A church with nothing gives nothing: a village can still go hungry."),
		Wiki.p("If you have almost no coins (%d or fewer) you can ask the church for food yourself, once a day: talk to the preacher and choose Ask the church for food. It gives up to %d pieces of what it holds." % [int(c.ask_player_max_coins), int(c.ask_player_units)]),
		Wiki.h("Alms"),
		Wiki.p("Offerings keep the clergy, and what is left goes as alms to the poorest. On the service day, after the clergy are paid, the chapel keeps back a modest reserve: about %d days of the clergy's wages, anything it owes them, and what it has lately been spending on relief food and seed. Everything above that is given in coins to the poorest households. A household is judged by everything it has, its coins, its shop's till and the food and firewood it holds, against what its food and firewood cost for two weeks: a larder of grain does not pay the rent or buy firewood, so a household with food but no coins can still be helped, while a household with plenty in store gets nothing even on a day it is short of coins. The poorest for each mouth they feed come first, each is given up to what it lacks, once, and what cannot be given stays in the chapel for next week. You are not given alms: you can ask the church for food instead (below)." % int(c.operating_reserve_days)),
		Wiki.h("The church's plot"),
		Wiki.p("The plot is ploughed, sown and harvested like any family's field, by the same rules, and all its harvest goes into the chapel's store to be given as relief. Pious villagers with time to spare (the old, and those out of work) may volunteer to work it, and so may the very devout after their day's work; at most %d at a time. You can volunteer too: face a cell of the church's field and Use to harvest, sow (the church's seed, or your own), till or clear it, by the same rules and in the time and stamina the work takes on your own field. The crop goes to the church's store for relief; you are paid nothing and take nothing, though the work trains your Farming as it does anyone's. A badly hurt person cannot work it. When nobody volunteers, the clergy work the plot themselves. The church buys its seed with its fund, from the farmers and the food merchant." % int(c.volunteers_max)),
		Wiki.h("The law"),
		Wiki.p("The preacher also teaches the law, as the reeve does but further: one lesson a day, up to level %d (see the skills)." % int(Law.cfg().teachers.preacher)),
		Wiki.links(["sys:manor_treasury", "sys:farmland"])], "chapel church preacher clergy offering donation alms relief charity volunteer plot assistant")
